# Wave W17-V (Route 208): rest stone — a foothill rest rock on the rest meadow: a broad flat-topped boulder in warm grey stone with a sunlit top face, set where the file of travellers stretches (design: foothill rest rocks line the bends, flat enough to sit on). On rest turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from the fleet’s posts by form entire and from shipped rock dressing by the flat worked top: this stone was placed, and sat on, for generations.
